{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1281329-v5-active-tremere-after-vienna-s-fall","id":1281329,"title":"[V5] - Active Tremere after Vienna's Fall","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-01-17T11:24:14-08:00","id":1281329,"title":"[V5] - Active Tremere after Vienna's Fall","content":"I am compiling a list of publicly known Tremere (at least, to members of the Clan) to give an idea of how they were impacted by Vienna's Fall, which my players are interested in investigating. I adopted this plot from V5, but made it more conspicuous and secretive (no televised attacks, only those who keep up with the SI know something happened). Only upper echelons of the Camarilla and the current Tremere leaders know the Clan has been crippled and broken, but try to keep a facade of normalcy (which is certainly not difficult to see through if one pays attention). <br /> <br /> I'm also assuming Vienna was an inside job to deal with the Great White Worm, but not all Councilors might have been aware of the coup. I think Meerlinda sacrificed her close ally and former friend Etrius, and those close to him, because they would not let go of a stratified Tremere Clan subservient to the Great White Worm. I don't think Meerlinda supports any V5 faction of the Clan, despite what Schrekt or Carna would claim. She has not made her survival of Vienna known yet, in my game.<br /> <br /> I realize my choices are somewhat arbitrary. I included some notes that might interest my players: some of this information will come in-game from a former Dark Ages Ceoris member - hence the inclusion of long lost vampires that this source would know. <br /> <br /> Any opinions or suggestions are welcome! Did I miss some important Tremere? Have I got the wrong information? (Some are from the Wiki). Would you select different members to fall/survive? <br /> <br /> <b><u>Inner Council</u></b><br /> <b>Etrius</b> \u2013 Eastern Europe Councilor. <i>Destroyed in Vienna</i>.<br /> <b>Grimgroth</b> \u2013 Western Europe Councilor. Has a long history and major enmity with the Order of Hermes, taking part in the Modern Massasa War. <i>Might have defected to the Sabbat, or destroyed in Vienna.</i><br /> <b>Meerlinda</b> \u2013 North America Councilor. <i>Hiding</i>. <br /> <b>Xavier de Cincao </b>\u2013 Latin America Councilor. Destroyed in his Chantry in Caracas in the late 20<sup>th</sup>c. <i>Replaced?</i><br /> <b>Abetorius</b> \u2013 Middle East Councilor, a Child of Meerlinda. <i>Either destroyed or hiding in Constantinople, where he once was Regent</i>.<br /> <b>Thomas Wyncham</b> \u2013 Far East Councilor, British. Second Councilor responsible for Asia, living in Hong Kong in the 1990s. Unknown location since his Childe, Oliver Thrace, defected to the Quincunx. <i>Wyncham might have been destroyed in Vienna, or is hiding in Asia</i>.<br /> <b>Elaine de Calinot</b> \u2013 Africa Councilor, disappeared in her Chantry in Algiers in the late 20<sup>th</sup>c. <i>Replaced?</i><br /> <br /> <b><u>Fallen in Vienna</u></b> (either close to Etrius or prominent enough to have been called to Vienna)<br /> <b>Astrid Thomas </b>\u2013 Etrius\u2019 child, High Regent of the Vienna Chantry. D<i>estroyed in Vienna with her Sire</i>.<br /> <b>Ulugh Begh</b> \u2013 Childe of Meerlinda, Embraced in 1253, Pontifex of the Balkans under Etrius since 1992. Founder of the Children of the Pyramid, leader of the Elite, a Quaesitor and great Salubri hunter. Justicar wanna-be, probably Archon. <i>Destroyed in Vienna.</i><br /> <b>John Diamond</b> \u2013 Childe of Meerlinda. USA Pontifex. <i>Destroyed in Vienna.</i><br /> <b>Peter Dorfman </b>\u2013 USA Pontifex and Regent of the Washington DC Chantry. <i>Destroyed in Vienna.</i><br /> <b>Nicolai Antonescu</b> \u2013 Primogen and Regent of the Chicago Chantry. <i>Destroyed in Vienna.</i><br /> <b>Gabrielle di Righetti</b> \u2013 Tremere Justicar around 1987, when she declared Dylan Bruce an Anathema and appointed his name to the Red List. At that ceremony, her Quaesitor was Pontifex Johannes Dee, and her witness was Petrodon. <i>Destroyed in Vienna.</i><br /> <b>Augustine d\u2019Erlette </b>\u2013 Childe of Celestyn. Master librarian of Vienna.<i> Destroyed in Vienna.</i><br /> <b>Claas Drescher</b> \u2013 Childe of Ardan Lane, active in Ceoris and Eastern Europe. Sire of former Justicar di Zagreb. Founder of the Krakow Chantry. <i>Destroyed in Vienna.</i><br /> <b>LeDuc</b> \u2013 one of the original Council of Seven. Once Regent of Paris, stepped down in 1133 for Goratrix and traveled to the Levant (to hunt Salubri?). <i>Destroyed in Vienna.</i><br /> <b>Ardan Lane</b> \u2013 Childe of Celestyn, held power in Romania and administered the abandoned Ceoris at least until WWII.<i> Destroyed in Vienna. </i><br /> <b>John Dee</b> \u2013 Childe of Meerlinda. Regent of the former London Chantry and former Pontifex of the British Isles. <i>Probably fell in London, or was destroyed in Vienna. </i><br /> <br /> <b><u>Active Camarilla</u></b> (known to be active, or held a title that would allow to become local leader, but not to be called to Vienna)<br /> <b>Karl Schrekt</b> \u2013 Grandchilde of Etrius, Child of Lotharius, and former Justicar. Current leader of Camarilla Tremere traditionalists.<br /> <b>Carna </b>\u2013 former Regent and Primogen of Milwaukee and one-time Prince of Marseilles. Current leader of House Carna, a splinter group from the main Clan with sympathies to the Anarch Movement. Officially still Camarilla.<br /> <b>Fanchon </b>\u2013 Founder of the Camarilla. Inner Circle. Unknown whereabouts.<br /> <b>Anastaz di Zagreb </b>\u2013 Childe of Claas Drescher. Justicar elected from 1998 to 2011. Was active against the Sabbat in Montreal.<br /> <b>Ian Carfax </b>\u2013 Long-time Archon of Justicar Schrekt. Current Tremere Justicar. <br /> <b>Lady Aisling Sturbridge </b>\u2013 High Regent of the Chantry of the Five Boroughs in New York.<br /> <b>Lord Ephraim Wainwright</b> \u2013 Regent of the Kenilworth Chantry in New York City.<br /> <b>Eugenio Estevez</b> \u2013 Regent of the Maupassant Room Chantry in New York City.<br /> <b>Dr. Mortius </b>\u2013 was stationed within the Milwaukee chantry, translated the Book of the Grave War. Unknown whereabouts.<br /> <b>Patricia von Bernstein</b> \u2013 Primogen of Frakfurt, secret head of the Order of the Wyrm. Infernalist, has access to a Pit.<br /> <b>Maxwell Ldescu </b>- Childe of Schrekt, former Primogen of West Berlin. Regent of the Berlin Chantry.<br /> <b>Tom\u00e1s Marcello</b> \u2013 Childe of Xavier de Cincao. Prince of Caracas.<br /> <b>Abigail</b> \u2013 Regent of the Miami Chantry and Sire of Hannah<br /> <b>Hannah</b> \u2013 Primogen and the Regent of the Atlanta Chantry. She also acted as an Harpy. Might have survived a rumored assassination attempt. <i>Currently inactive.</i><br /> <b>Luna Demian</b> \u2013 current Regent of the San Francisco Chantry.<br /> <b>Abraham DuSable</b> \u2013 current Regent of the Chicago Chantry.<br /> <b>Lille Haake</b> \u2013 Primogen and Regent of the Amsterdam Chantry.<br /> <b>Sylvia Kilver</b> \u2013 member of the Cairo Chantry, a slave of the Setite sorcereress Kahina.<br /> <b>Hypatia</b> \u2013 Regent of the Cairo Chantry, slave of the Dream Court Mathuselah.<br /> <b>Valois Sang</b> \u2013 Camarilla agent within Montreal. His Sire was the Prince of Quebec. <i>Active?</i><br /> <b>Maximillian Strauss</b> \u2013 Primogen in Los Angeles and Regent of the local Chantry during the brief time the Camarilla had taken control in 2004. Left LA by 2005.<br /> <b>Bourdona</b> \u2013 Sire of Carna. Prince of Marseille.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Independent</u></b><br /> <b>Therimna</b> \u2013 Childe of Goratrix, known as Ute Kovacs in modern nights. Was one of the first Tremere and one of the developers of Thaumaturgical Alchemy. She is an apostate of her Clan and acts as a mercenary under the guise of a Tzimisce.<br /> <b>Theresa Kymena</b> \u2013 Salubri sympathizer. Regent of the Constatinople Chantry until the Fourth Crusade. Created Dream Magic. Her future fate is unknown.<br /> <b>Ponticulus</b> \u2013 a mage of the House Tremere, and one of the closest advisors of the founder of that house. He died in 980 during the ritual of consecration of Ceoris, but later returned as a wraith. <i>Might still haunt Ceoris</i>.<br /> <b>Virstania</b> \u2013 Creator and Mistress of Gargoyles among clan Tremere. She helped them to revolt. Unknown whereabouts.<br /> <b>Celestyn</b> \u2013 knowledgeable of Saulot and Kupala. <i>Either was destroyed in Vienna, or is hiding in Asia</i>.<br /> <b>Oliver Thrace</b> \u2013 Child of Wyncham, defected to the Quincunx. Infernalist.<br /> <b>Wan Zhu</b> \u2013 Child of Thrace, fled her Sire to SF and joined the New Promise Mandarinate there, against the Camarilla.<br /> <b>Valerius Maior</b> \u2013 Antitribu who survived the destruction in Mexico. He is part of the Red List, formerly the third Anathema and recently re-evaluated to the fourth. Infernalist. Childe of Mistress Fanchon.<br /> <b>Kyoko Shinsegawa</b> \u2013 placed on the Camarilla's Red List following the death of Genina.<br /> <b>Rutor</b> \u2013 Childe of Jervais, tried to be Prince of Copenhagen. Member of the Red Sign.<br /> <b>Epistatia</b> - Eldest Childe of Goratrix (E.1022) and the first outside of Council of Seven to be Embraced. Amnesiac and estranged from the vampire society since the first Massasa War.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Active Anarch</u></b><br /> <b>Monica Chang</b> \u2013 an Anarch sympathizer, part of the Digital Draculas. Originally from Hong Kong, Chang was Embraced in the 1880s. After being transferred to Washington DC, she stole most of her Clan's research on Technomancy and fled to Chicago, to the Ventrue hacker known as Hurricane.<br /> <b>Maldavis</b> \u2013 currently active in Chicago<br /> <b>Masika St. John</b> \u2013 creator of the Technomancy. Whereabouts unknown.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Sabbat</u></b><br /> <b>Goratrix</b> \u2013 House Goratrix leader, possessed by Tremere (Sabbat?).<br /> <b>Heinrich Himmler </b>\u2013 Childe of Ldescu, was unbondable and defected to the Antitribu, but was also Primogen in East Berlin until the Blood Curse in 1997, after which he left. <i>Possibly destroyed in 1998 in Mexico. </i><br /> <b>Paul Cordwood</b> \u2013 Childe of Epistatia, vanished during the Gargoyle Revolt; rumors claim that he joined the Tremere antitribu and acts as a Bishop of the Sabbat.<i> Possibly destroyed in 1998 in Mexico. </i><br /> <b>Deverra</b> \u2013 head of the Telyavelic Tremere of Lithuania and part of the inner circle of the Gangrel Khan Qarakh. Deverra sacrificed herself to Etrius allow the other members of her coven to escape. Her remains were ritually preserved and taken to Ceoris. <i>Might be behind the Telyavs, or has a Childe who is.</i><br /> <b>Orlando Oriundus</b> \u2013 Childe of Goratrix. Became Tremere Antitribu and attained the title of Bishop within the Sabbat. <i>Possibly destroyed in 1998 in Mexico. </i><br /> <b>Malgorzata</b> \u2013 Childe of Goratrix, and the leader of the Conspirator Faction. Captured in Ceoris in the 1570s by Tzimisce anarchs during a raid. Taken prisoner and tortured, she revealed all she knew about Ceoris' defenses and Tremere's plans. Goratrix found her several horrific decades later, but left her there to linger. <i>Malgorzata is described as a Sabbat Priscus in VTE, which I like.</i><br /> <b>Elena Mendoza Vasquez</b> \u2013 Regent of the Mexico City Chantry. Destroyed in 1998 in Mexico. <br /> <br /> <b><u>Long Lost</u></b><br /> <b>Jervais</b> \u2013 Childe of Malgorzata. Responsible for the destruction of the Telyavelics. In 1931, Jervais met destruction at the hand of Spanish Republicans while on a visit there. Rumors are that the attack happened at Goratrix's behest. Alternatively, destroyed in an attack against Hunedoara in the 1500s.<br /> <b>Lotharius</b> \u2013 Childe of Etrius, once Prince of Vienna and last Pontifex of Austria, destroyed by an Assamite in 1529. Sire of Karl Schrekt.<br /> <b>Mendacamina</b> \u2013 Childe of Etrius, loyal to Goratrix and mage hunter of Ceoris. Was Regent of the Vienna Chantry from 1232 to 1230, heavily involved in the Massasa War of the time. Destroyed in 1284 by Etrius.<br /> <b>Curaferrum </b>\u2013 was the castellan of Ceoris and a loyal servant of Etrius. When the Gargoyle Revolt hit the chantry Curaferrum was diablerized by their leader Virstania.<br /> <b>Bitiurges</b> \u2013 Childe of Etrius, was Antitribu during the 18<sup>th</sup> and 19<sup>th</sup> c. Destroyed in 1977 in Germany.<br /> <b>Edward Bainbridge</b> \u2013 Childe of Elaine of Calinot, was Primogen of London during the Victorian Era. <i>Probably killed before the 20<sup>th </sup>c</i>.<br /> <b>Nickolai</b> - survivor of the Tremere antitribu massacre in Mexico City. The killer of Justicar Petrodon. Sire of Leopold. Had the Eye of Hazimel. Destroyed by the Camarilla in NY in 1999.<br /> <b>Lord Casmir</b> - a member of the Conspiracy of Isaac. Destroyed sometime before 1848 (probably much earlier).<br /> <b>Andre Malotte</b> \u2013 was active in London. Was responsible for and destroyed in the Great Fire. Was one of the minor conspirators in the Conspiracy of Isaac. Had the Sargon Fragment.<br /> <b>Helena Taylor</b> \u2013 former Regent of the Washington D.C. Chantry. Her fate following the Sabbat assault on the city in 1999 is unknown.<br /> <b>Kasper Von Aupfholme</b> \u2013 Childe of Mooreau. Sire of Hypatia. Former Councilor of Africa. Disappeared.<br /> <b>Preston Varrick</b> - former Regent of Tokyo. Perished in Hunedoara.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T12:32:38-08:00","id":1281344,"title":"","content":"Although it is known that Maldavis is a childe of Abraham DuSable, she is considered Caitiff.<br /> <br /> There's one particular Tremere that always intrigued me. Lucidus, the only one to ever defeat Tremere while they were both mages (he is mentioned in HoT).<br /> <br /> -Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1594,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","user":"Saga","date":". 01-17-2019, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T14:32:18-08:00","id":1281375,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1594_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1594\" data-vbnamecard=\"1594\">Saga</a> <br /> <br /> Thanks for the reminder regarding Maldavis! <br /> <br /> And although I did read HoT, I don't recall Lucidus. Was he ever Embraced? I'll have to look.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T15:47:26-08:00","id":1281386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>valismedsen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1281329-v5-active-tremere-after-vienna-s-fall?p=1281375#post1281375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> <br /> <br /> Thanks for the reminder regarding Maldavis! <br /> <br /> And although I did read HoT, I don't recall Lucidus. Was he ever Embraced? I'll have to look.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pg.137 and no, he was never mentioned again. Perhaps he got embraced by Ala after all, but the background potential is huge for him. I usually take that he was the only one to be personally embraced by Tremere and he is the only one capable of restoring order if he fails to control Saulot's soul within him.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T20:23:53-08:00","id":1281439,"title":"","content":"This my assumption, but in the anarch write-up of house ipsissimus, I thought the Xbor5 username in the chat refered to Xavier de Cincao. Personal thought was that he faked his death and is now owned by the Drowned, like the mad monk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23964-el-barto","name":"El Barto","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T05:46:41-08:00","id":1281494,"title":"","content":"Amazing headcanons, El Barto and Saga! I'll steal from you both! Thanks!<br /> <br /> Edit: Hey, El Barto, any ideas on who DrMagus speaking with Xbor5 would be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":412,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","user":"valismedsen","date":". 01-18-2019, 09:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T09:48:41-08:00","id":1281525,"title":"","content":"Could be Dr. John Dee, but like you wrote, him being destroyed in London is truth until proven otherwise. Best bet is Dr. Mortius, original translator of the Book of Grave-War who just... disappeared from society a few years before Carna broke from the pyramid.<br /> <br /> My headcanon is that he helped Shrekt guide the SI to Vienna so there were free Tremere he could collect into a house without painting a bullseye on himself like Carna - that he waited till there was something like Ipsissimus before helping found Ipsissimus. She's a true believer. He's a more wily one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23964-el-barto","name":"El Barto","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T11:12:18-08:00","id":1281537,"title":"","content":"I like it! Going to steal that too!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T01:38:49-08:00","id":1283467,"title":"","content":"Thank you for posting this list. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>valismedsen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1281329-v5-active-tremere-after-vienna-s-fall#post1281329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am compiling a list of publicly known Tremere (at least, to members of the Clan) to give an idea of how they were impacted by Vienna's Fall, which my players are interested in investigating. (...)<br /> <b><u>Inner Council</u></b><br /> <b>Etrius</b> \u2013 Eastern Europe Councilor. <i>Destroyed in Vienna</i>.<br /> <b>Grimgroth</b> \u2013 Western Europe Councilor. Has a long history and major enmity with the Order of Hermes, taking part in the Modern Massasa War. <i>Might have defected to the Sabbat, or destroyed in Vienna.</i><br /> <b>Meerlinda</b> \u2013 North America Councilor. <i>Hiding</i>.<br /> <b>Xavier de Cincao </b>\u2013 Latin America Councilor. Destroyed in his Chantry in Caracas in the late 20<sup>th</sup>c. <i>Replaced?</i><br /> <b>Abetorius</b> \u2013 Middle East Councilor, a Child of Meerlinda. <i>Either destroyed or hiding in Constantinople, where he once was Regent</i>.<br /> <b>Thomas Wyncham</b> \u2013 Far East Councilor, British. Second Councilor responsible for Asia, living in Hong Kong in the 1990s. Unknown location since his Childe, Oliver Thrace, defected to the Quincunx. <i>Wyncham might have been destroyed in Vienna, or is hiding in Asia</i>.<br /> <b>Elaine de Calinot</b> \u2013 Africa Councilor, disappeared in her Chantry in Algiers in the late 20<sup>th</sup>c. <i>Replaced?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>About Elaine de Calinot it is written on the White Wolf Wiki : &quot;Her detractors are quick to point out that Elaine herself has been unreachable in recent months from her Chantry in Algiers; they point to this as proof of the foolishness of her plan. There are rumors, however, that Elaine has simply entered a new phase of her plan. She is said to be travelling throughout her territory seeking out those who show both magical and leadership potential.&quot; . I don't think there is enough indication to consider that anything harmful or greatly detrimental happened to her.<br /> <br /> Which of the statuses of the Inner Councilors in this list are based on anything written in V5 books ? As in, is it written in V5 that Etrius was surely destroyed in Vienna, and that Meerlinda certainly survived the recent events ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 01-29-2019, 04:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T16:24:40-08:00","id":1283591,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3254_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3254\" data-vbnamecard=\"3254\">Muad'Dib</a> You're welcome for the list! Also, as far as I know, we haven't seen any official word on the fate of the Inner Council in V5. These are the plots I'm using in my game, although beside hypothesizing the fate of the Inner Council I tried to stay true to canon. Sorry if I wasn't clear on that. Regarding Elaine de Calinot, I think the text from the Wiki comes from the first Clanbook Tremere, the first and only time we heard from this Councilor, aside from some information that can be implied in Cairo and London by Night books - as far as I know. That was quite some time ago both in-game and out. But I also like the idea of her surviving and hiding (or perhaps imprisoned) among the Laibon!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T18:22:39-08:00","id":1283609,"title":"","content":"With so many high ranking Tremere being destroyed, now would actually be a great time for Elaine de Calinot to make a reappearance with some kind of special result from her activities in Africa. I\u2019ve actually been wondering about her ever since I originally read her description in the first Clanbook Tremere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T19:08:07-08:00","id":1283618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1281329-v5-active-tremere-after-vienna-s-fall?p=1283609#post1283609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With so many high ranking Tremere being destroyed, now would actually be a great time for Elaine de Calinot to make a reappearance with some kind of special result from her activities in Africa. I\u2019ve actually been wondering about her ever since I originally read her description in the first Clanbook Tremere.</div> </div> </div> </div>She could return to the Jyhad with some (in-universe) game-changing knowledge gained by studying the Laibon's generation-adjusting rites.<br /> I mean, if they supposedly increase their childer's generation that way, an ambitious entrepeneur could find a way to turn that magic upside down...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23964-el-barto","name":"El Barto","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-30T06:33:14-08:00","id":1283702,"title":"","content":"Great ideas, people! Keep them coming!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-30T13:56:44-08:00","id":1283790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>El Barto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1281329-v5-active-tremere-after-vienna-s-fall?p=1283618#post1283618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> She could return to the Jyhad with some (in-universe) game-changing knowledge gained by studying the Laibon's generation-adjusting rites.<br /> I mean, if they supposedly increase their childer's generation that way, an ambitious entrepeneur could find a way to turn that magic upside down...</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. She may actually come back wanting to rule over the Clan. She was a member of the Inner Council and is 4th generation. I could see her having a good argument for being in charge. Especially if she has some special kind of potent magic that no one else in the Clan has, in addition to the insane magical might that a 4th generation Tremere elder is going to have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-30T18:18:17-08:00","id":1283828,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1129_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1129\" data-vbnamecard=\"1129\">Sergeant Brother</a> Completely agreed!<br /> <br /> Although I should point that London by Night's Victorian Tremere Primogen, Edward Brainbridge, a direct Childe of Elaine, is 7th Generation. He was Embraced in 1850 when she was one of Africa's 7 Pontifices.<br /> <br /> Cairo by Night states she replaced Mooreau, whose Childe Von Aupfholme was 8th Generation and Embraced in the late 18th century some years after the disappearance of the first Councilor Mooreau replaced. Curiously, Mooreau is said to have been reassigned soon after, not dead or missing. It seems the Tremere did not bother to send very powerful members to Africa. This would make Elaine the third Councilor for Africa, from the early 1800s until the late 1990s. Elaine is also said to be a French noblewoman. I wonder if she could be a Grandchild of Goratrix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T06:24:46-08:00","id":1283904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>valismedsen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1281329-v5-active-tremere-after-vienna-s-fall?p=1283591#post1283591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry if I wasn't clear on that. Regarding Elaine de Calinot, I think the text from the Wiki comes from the first Clanbook Tremere, the first and only time we heard from this Councilor, aside from some information that can be implied in Cairo and London by Night books - as far as I know. That was quite some time ago both in-game and out. But I also like the idea of her surviving and hiding (or perhaps imprisoned) among the Laibon!</div> </div> </div> </div>Elaine de Calinot is also described in &quot;<i>Encyclopedia Vampirica</i>&quot; on page 60.<br /> Does anyone know if this is an official illustration of her ? <a href=\"http://porteddieux.clicforum.com/t1246-La-Maison-de-Calinot.htm\" target=\"_blank\">http://porteddieux.clicforum.com/t12...de-Calinot.htm</a> ( I assume it is from the first Clanbook Tremere ) . She is one of my favourite V:tM characters just because of this illustration, even if there is very little information about her. It puts across &quot;One of the most knowledgable and powerful Thaumaturgists and occultists in the world.&quot; perfectly, while maintaining focus on Elaine de Calinot as a person at the same time. Though, in regard depicting members of the Council of Seven, the illiustration of Thomas Wyncham is a close second, in it's relative simplicity. And of course the illustration of Meerlinda ( The one in which she has flowers in her hair. Does anyone know from which book it is ? ) is distinctly appropriate for an Inner Councilor, and she looks gorgeous in it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>valismedsen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1281329-v5-active-tremere-after-vienna-s-fall?p=1283828#post1283828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although I should point that London by Night's Victorian Tremere Primogen, Edward Brainbridge, a direct Childe of Elaine, is 7th Generation. He was Embraced in 1850 when she was one of Africa's 7 Pontifices.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like how in this Embrace story Elaine de Calinot fed semi-openly on a community. Usually when a person encounters a Vampire preying on mundane humans in this way, it is a local Vampire ; and usually it is a Gangrel or a Nosferatu. That a Pontifex of the Clan Tremere did this is a distinct reminder of the variety and possibilities in the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>valismedsen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1281329-v5-active-tremere-after-vienna-s-fall?p=1283591#post1283591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You're welcome for the list! Also, as far as I know, we haven't seen any official word on the fate of the Inner Council in V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>So all that is written is that the Vienna Chantry ( or the main part of it ? ) got destroyed ? Is anything written about any Tremere Vampires being destroyed during this ?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>valismedsen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1281329-v5-active-tremere-after-vienna-s-fall#post1281329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did I miss some important Tremere?</div> </div> </div> </div>You didn't write the status of Tremere himself. I consider the idea / plot that his body turned into a giant white worm to be ridiculous \u2013 surely the other Tremere Vampires would be able to help in regard to something like this. It makes more sense as a lie that somebody put into circulation to make other Vampires distrust and doubt Clan Tremere. I think that it is much more interesting if Tremere is fine and involved in various matters and plots during the modern nights.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 01-31-2019, 09:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T08:49:19-08:00","id":1283934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1281329-v5-active-tremere-after-vienna-s-fall?p=1283904#post1283904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elaine de Calinot is also described in &quot;<i>Encyclopedia Vampirica</i>&quot; on page 60.<br /> Does anyone know if this is an official illustration of her ? <a href=\"http://porteddieux.clicforum.com/t1246-La-Maison-de-Calinot.htm\" target=\"_blank\">http://porteddieux.clicforum.com/t12...de-Calinot.htm</a> ( I assume it is from the first Clanbook Tremere ) .<br /> She is one of my favourite V:tM characters just because of this illustration, even if there is very little information about her. It puts across &quot;One of the most knowledgable and powerful Thaumaturgists and occultists in the world.&quot; perfectly, while maintaining focus on Elaine de Calinot as a person at the same time. Though, in regard depicting members of the Council of Seven, the illiustration of Thomas Wyncham is a close second, in it's relative simplicity. And of course the illustration of Meerlinda ( The one in which she has flowers in her hair. Does anyone know from which book it is ? ) is distinctly appropriate for an Inner Councilor, and she looks gorgeous in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>All these images come from the first Clanbook. They were all great! Aside from Etrius in some books (mainly in Children of the Inquisition and House of Tremere) and Meerlinda dressed in a maid's veil, in the British Isles DA book, those are the only images of the Councilors that I am aware of. Elaine's certainly is one of the most striking, although Meerlinda's is still my favorite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1281329-v5-active-tremere-after-vienna-s-fall?p=1283904#post1283904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like how in this Embrace story Elaine de Calinot fed semi-openly on a community. Usually when a person encounters a Vampire preying on mundane humans in this way, it is a local Vampire ; and usually it is a Gangrel or a Nosferatu. That a Pontifex of the Clan Tremere did this is a distinct reminder of the variety and possibilities in the World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point! And that took place in Congo, quite far from the Chantry in Algiers from where she disappeared in the 20th c. Interestingly, Congo is the place the Laibon Lasombra Xi Dundu originally hailed from. Their expulsion was quite spectacular, and as I read it, would already have happened in the time of Brainbridge's Embrace. Wondering if Elaine was investigating something to do with that. Starting to picture her character sheet now, in V5, with both Blood Sorcery and Oblivion. Which is quite awesome!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1281329-v5-active-tremere-after-vienna-s-fall?p=1283904#post1283904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So all that is written is that the Vienna Chantry ( or the main part of it ? ) got destroyed ? Is anything written about any Tremere Vampires being destroyed during this ?</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I understood, it is implied most of the Tremere placed high in the Pyramid were in Vienna and were destroyed. The Chantry was destroyed in live television, in what was blamed, by the very SI, as a major terrorist attack. I think there were missiles involved, or at least explosions, as well as a ground attack team during the day. And those aware of the SI say Tremere magic failed or was countered. There are no confirmed deaths, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1281329-v5-active-tremere-after-vienna-s-fall?p=1283904#post1283904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You didn't write the status of Tremere himself. I consider the idea / plot that his body turned into a giant white worm to be ridiculous \u2013 surely the other Tremere Vampires would be able to help in regard to something like this. It makes more sense as a lie that somebody put into circulation to make other Vampires distrust and doubt Clan Tremere. I think that it is much more interesting if Tremere is fine and involved in various matters and plots during the modern nights.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, I forgot Tremere himself, although I like the canon: that he is in Goratrix's body; the Great White Worm (or Tremere's original body anyway) is now host to Saulot's P'o (or his awakened Beast, or Shadow - these are effectively all the same for me); and his Hun or Humanity is (or was) in Hunedoara.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T10:20:07-08:00","id":1283962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>valismedsen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1281329-v5-active-tremere-after-vienna-s-fall?p=1283934#post1283934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All these images come from the first Clanbook. They were all great! Aside from Etrius in some books (mainly in Children of the Inquisition and House of Tremere) and Meerlinda dressed in a maid's veil, in the British Isles DA book, those are the only images of the Councilors that I am aware of. Elaine's certainly is one of the most striking, although Meerlinda's is still my favorite.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Good point! And that took place in Congo, quite far from the Chantry in Algiers from where she disappeared in the 20th c. Interestingly, Congo is the place the Laibon Lasombra Xi Dundu originally hailed from. Their expulsion was quite spectacular, and as I read it, would already have happened in the time of Brainbridge's Embrace. Wondering if Elaine was investigating something to do with that. Starting to picture her character sheet now, in V5, with both Blood Sorcery and Oblivion. Which is quite awesome!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As far as I understood, it is implied most of the Tremere placed high in the Pyramid were in Vienna and were destroyed. The Chantry was destroyed in live television, in what was blamed, by the very SI, as a major terrorist attack. I think there were missiles involved, or at least explosions, as well as a ground attack team during the day. And those aware of the SI say Tremere magic failed or was countered. There are no confirmed deaths, though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> True, I forgot Tremere himself, although I like the canon: that he is in Goratrix's body; the Great White Worm (or Tremere's original body anyway) is now host to Saulot's P'o (or his awakened Beast, or Shadow - these are effectively all the same for me); and his Hun or Humanity is (or was) in Hunedoara.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically it's not canon, since V20 was self-proclaimed &quot;canon agnostic&quot;.<br /> <br /> Canon is that Tzimisce kicked them both (but, you know, Golden Rule).<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T10:36:09-08:00","id":1283965,"title":"","content":"Beckett's Jyhad Diary is canon, though, right? It was announced as a bridge from V20 to V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T11:20:22-08:00","id":1283971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>valismedsen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1281329-v5-active-tremere-after-vienna-s-fall?p=1283965#post1283965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beckett's Jyhad Diary is canon, though, right? It was announced as a bridge from V20 to V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only V5 can confirm such a thing, but I think they do. Yet, that renders V20 &quot;canon agnostic&quot; as a lie.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1594,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","user":"Saga","date":". 01-31-2019, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T11:17:02-08:00","id":1284173,"title":"","content":"I was thinking how local Tremere factions might rise around strong leaders with power and charisma to establish their own houses. <br /> <br /> Based on the list of possible active members I compiled, and the very helpful contributions on this thread, I was thinking about adding rumors about the existence of the following Houses in my game:<br /> <br /> <u>V5 Official</u><br /> <b>House Tremere</b> \u2013 Camarilla, led by Schrekt. Traditionalist Tremere magic.<br /> <b>House Goratrix</b> \u2013 Sabbat, led by Goratrix (or Tremere in Goratrix's body). Specializes in unorthodox magic. <br /> <b>House Carna</b> - officially Camarilla with Independent and Anarch sympathies, led by Carna. Witchcraft.<br /> <b>House Ipsimus</b> \u2013 Anarch. Crowley inspired mysticism, possibly led by the vampire Crowley (was a Malkavian in A World of Darkness 1st Ed, might be a much older deluded Malkavian from London by Night)<br /> <br /> <u>V20 Semi-official</u><br /> <b>House Telyavel</b> \u2013 Sabbat, could possibly have independent members. No official leader, could be a descendant of their DA leader Deverra. Telyavelic magic. <br /> <b>Digital Draculas aka Hacktivists</b> \u2013 Anarch. Unknown leader(s), maybe Masinka St. John? Probably accepts non-Tremere members. Technomancy.<br /> <b>House Trimira</b> \u2013 India based, officially Camarilla. Unknown leaders. Accepts non-Tremere members. Sadhana.<br /> <br /> <u>Rumors in my game</u><br /> <b>House Calinot </b>\u2013 African based, local Camarilla and Laibon courts. Officially Independent. Led by Elaine de Calinot. Laibon magic.<br /> <b>House Cincao</b> \u2013 Latin American based, local Camarilla and Sabbat. Led by Xavier de Cincao (or his Drowned Masters?). Might be a front for the Drowned Legacies. Specializes in Latin American magical traditions.<br /> <b>House Virstania</b> \u2013 Independent. Led by Virstania. Mostly composed of Virstania and her Gargoyles. Gargoyle creation.<br /> <b>House Trismegistus</b> \u2013 Camarilla. Dr John Dee (or someone assuming his identity). Composed of former members of the Elite, Trismegistus, Hashem and Quaesitori factions. Kabbalah and Angelic (demonic?) summoning. Might be infernal. <br /> <b>House Yomi</b> \u2013 Quincux and other Kuei-Jin courts. Led by Oliver Thrace. Kuei-Jin and Akuma magic. Infernal.<br /> <b>House of the Dream</b> \u2013 Istanbul based, officially Camarilla. Led by Thereza Kymena, composed of former members of the Brothers of Absinthe and the Third Eye factions. Salubri friendly. Reveres the new Trinity of Constantinople. Potentially infernal. <br /> <b>House of the Serpent</b> \u2013 Cairo based, officially Camarilla. Led by Kahina, composed of former members of the Eye of the Serpent faction and allows non-Tremere members, mainly Setite/Ministry. Akhu.<br /> <b>House Auram</b> \u2013 officially Camarilla, with Independent and Sabbat sympathies. Led by Therimna, composed if former members of the Auram Guild faction. Specializes in Alchemy.<br /> <b>House Liban</b> \u2013 France based, officially Independent. Led by a descendant of Mathieu de Calice, composed of former members of the Humanus League and the Golden Path of Harmony factions. Golconda seekers, specializes in the goal of curing vampirism. <br /> <br /> Any other ideas for Houses of suggestion on these? Some of these could benefit from naming suggestions... <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T13:23:47-08:00","id":1284197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>valismedsen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1281329-v5-active-tremere-after-vienna-s-fall?p=1284173#post1284173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking how local Tremere factions might rise around strong leaders with power and charisma to establish their own houses.<br /> <br /> Based on the list of possible active members I compiled, and the very helpful contributions on this thread, I was thinking about adding rumors about the existence of the following Houses in my game:<br /> (...)<br /> <u>Rumors in my game</u><br /> <b>House Calinot </b>\u2013 African based, local Camarilla and Laibon courts. Officially Independent. Led by Elaine de Calinot. Laibon magic.<br /> <b>House Cincao</b> \u2013 Latin American based, local Camarilla and Sabbat. Led by Xavier de Cincao (or his Drowned Masters?). Might be a front for the Drowned Legacies. Specializes in Latin American magical traditions.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It is nice to see House Calinot included in a chronicle. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> What about House Meerlinda ? <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> It always made sense to me as possibility, because Meerlinda is one of the original Tremere Vampires, and one of the most capable, wise, and intelligent members of the Clan Tremere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>valismedsen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1281329-v5-active-tremere-after-vienna-s-fall#post1281329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Bitiurges</b> \u2013 Childe of Etrius, was Antitribu during the 18<sup>th</sup> and 19<sup>th</sup> c. Destroyed in 1977 in Germany.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you change the fate of Bitiurges in your chronicle ? I was so disappointed when I read that he got destroyed. Not only he has a nice description, he is also a Mage who chose the Embrace. And it is hilarious, in a macabre way, that Ponticulus went through so much effort to dictate to him that some Tremere Mages became Vampires ( and other information and ruminations ) , only for Bitiurges to read it, and decide to side with the Clan Tremere Vampires. Out of all the Mages in Ceoris, it just had to be Bitiurges that Ponticulus confided to. And this story is a good reminder to not assume that every person who isn't a Vampire will act against them ; and that some will decide to aid Vampires.<br /> <br /> Also - quite a conicidence, isn't it ? Maybe somebody influenced or guided Ponticulus into confiding to this particular person ; counting that Bitiurges would choose to become a Vampire, and that he would become one of low Generation and excellent initial standing. Maybe Bitiurges had \u2013 or still has \u2013 some part to play ? Or he was chosen for his potential as a Vampire, or potential as a Blood Magician ? Somebody might have deemed his upbringing ( coming from a line of Tremere Mages ) and personal traits interesting, worthwhile, unique, and valueable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>valismedsen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1281329-v5-active-tremere-after-vienna-s-fall?p=1283934#post1283934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All these images come from the first Clanbook. They were all great! Aside from Etrius in some books (mainly in Children of the Inquisition and House of Tremere) and Meerlinda dressed in a maid's veil, in the British Isles DA book, those are the only images of the Councilors that I am aware of. Elaine's certainly is one of the most striking, although Meerlinda's is still my favorite.</div> </div> </div> </div>If your storytelling involves matters of the Clan Tremere to a great extent, then I recommend that you re-read the description of Etrius in the second Clanbook Tremere. It is one of rare extensive descriptions of how a greatly capable and experienced Vampire thinks, makes choices, and organizes matters.<br /> <br /> Are any of your players' PCs Tremere Vampires ?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 02-01-2019, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T21:32:22-08:00","id":1284275,"title":"","content":"So what is up with Meerlinda these days?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T08:04:03-08:00","id":1284497,"title":"","content":"@<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib\">Muad'Dib</a> Thanks for the comments. And yes, I have a Tremere PC in my game, so this thread is helping me brainstorm some ideas that will directly affect this PC and the player.<br /> <br /> Regarding Meerlinda, in my game she's in hiding right now, being the main architect of Vienna's fall to get rid of Etrius and his obsession with Tremere as well as the horror that Tremere had become. What she'll do next I'm still pondering over. I'm thinking about giving her mortality back (and possibly her Avatar too), through the Red Sign. Always wanted to run that Chronicle!<br /> <br /> I should note that Meerlinda has helped the Tremere PC before in my game, so whatever affects Meerlinda will impact them both.<br /> <br /> Officially in V5, though, Meerlinda might have been destroyed in Vienna.<br /> <br /> Edited to add: I quite like the idea of Meerlinda leading a mortal House in the Order of Hermes. I don't think she would name the house after herself. Probably would name it House Tremere, to honor the memory of a once great man and mentor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":412,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","user":"valismedsen","date":". 02-03-2019, 11:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T11:16:36-08:00","id":1284545,"title":"","content":"Did consider the possibility of Meerlinda deciding to try to think and act following the ideals of high Humanity ( which she, and other greatly capable Tremere Vampires, don't follow, as far as I know ) ? The often mentioned low Humanity of the more influential and highly placed Vampires in the Camarilla always seemed to be too one-note for me. In regard to the Clan Tremere, I have thought about how trying to maintain high standards of compassion and morality can be a legitimate path in regard to mysticism, and the occult. I think that a person can gain something if they refuse to engage in harmful practices for the purpose of gaining knowledge or power ; such an attitude and decisions made can lead to advancing in mystical knowledge and capabilities. Meerlinda seems to be a Vampire who could relatively easily make successful arrangements and decisions to cause a shift in attitude towards higher Humanity, if not in the Camarilla, then just in the Clan Tremere ( at least at first ) .<br /> <br /> How numerous are House Goratrix and House Carna in your chronicle ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T16:08:55-08:00","id":1284599,"title":"","content":"I don't know exactly what to do with Carna and her followers. Pagan magic and witchcraft seems better served by the Telyavs, although I can see how both groups would have different approaches to Humanity and occupy different niches. Even if Carna is shown to be ruthless (the fiction intro for Blood Sorcery in V5, for instance), the Telyavs are Sabbat and supposedly much more sinister, aligned with a dark god or even a demon. While Carna is connected to the Book of the Grave War and can break blood bonds, so that might be what makes her truly unique. Still, I see her and her House as a pretty localized, american group, and maybe more successful with younger vampires. I guess in a scenario where so many leaders rise, Carna still has a seat at the table, but is just one of many now (as opposed to being one third of the whole Clan leadership, as in canon V5). <br /> <br /> Now, House Goratrix, and the man himself, are my golden children. I have a special place in my heart for that bastard! I actually want him to be rescued from that damn mirror and come back and kick Tremere's ass, and take his body and House back. Really, what even are Tremere's intentions? I guess House Goratrix (for now under Tremere's leadership) is steadily increasing in numbers in my game. The implication that Carna might also be under Tremere's influence is troubling, however. Will he burn all members of his Clan again? <br /> <br /> I truly agree that Meerlinda could represent a more humane approach to mysticism. Diplomacy and compromise in the face of adversity have been her hallmarks since ever, so I guess the civility of a more Human Tremere suits her and her would-be followers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T17:58:58-08:00","id":1284620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>valismedsen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1281329-v5-active-tremere-after-vienna-s-fall?p=1284599#post1284599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know exactly what to do with Carna and her followers. Pagan magic and witchcraft seems better served by the Telyavs,</div> </div> </div> </div>I take the paganism of Carna to be the modern ideas of neo-paganism. Which is to say, rather bloodless and family friendly in a liberal and feminist manner. The Telyavs practice actual paganism, which is bloody minded and not family friendly in the modern sense. That said, Carna's social circle of like-minded mortals is probably larger than that of the Telyavs. so each method is home to strengths and weaknesses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>valismedsen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1281329-v5-active-tremere-after-vienna-s-fall?p=1284599#post1284599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really, what even are Tremere's intentions?</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the major goals of Clan Tremere is discovering, and exploiting, the True Name of the entire human race. Following that is the secret behind why Meerlinda is in North America. In the old Gehenna source book, using that was a kind of last ditch effort by Tremere himself. At guess, he is doing something similar in V5. The various &quot;Tremere Houses&quot; give him options as he pursues his goal and for dealing with his many enemies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>valismedsen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1281329-v5-active-tremere-after-vienna-s-fall?p=1284599#post1284599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Diplomacy and compromise in the face of adversity have been her hallmarks since ever, so I guess the civility of a more Human Tremere suits her and her would-be followers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, that makes her people savy, the master manipulator of the original Tremere and someone capable of playing the long game. None of it speaks to her being humane. And there is nothing to say she would remain loyal to Tremere (the man or the clan) once she had the True Name of the entire human race.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T10:57:36-08:00","id":1284763,"title":"","content":"What was the plan to get all of Humanity's True Name again? I don't quite remember that plot, only that it existed. I do seem to recall being somewhat... meh. Like, was it compiling everybody's name who has ever been born or something like that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T16:16:44-08:00","id":1284826,"title":"","content":"The idea is if a caster possesses the True Name of a target, then the target cannot resist any magic or power used on them by the caster. So humanity would be at the feet of the Tremere. So would other vampires, including the Antedeluvians, because they had all once been human. As evil plans go, it is less showy than the goals of the Giovanni, but no less scary if you are paying attention.<br /> <br /> Meerlinda is directing the project, and working with the family tree and histories run by the Mormons out of Salt Lake City, and she is keeping tabs on the results of the humane genome project.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T21:59:07-08:00","id":1284890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1281329-v5-active-tremere-after-vienna-s-fall?p=1284826#post1284826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea is if a caster possesses the True Name of a target, then the target cannot resist any magic or power used on them by the caster. So humanity would be at the feet of the Tremere. So would other vampires, including the Antedeluvians, because they had all once been human. As evil plans go, it is less showy than the goals of the Giovanni, but no less scary if you are paying attention.<br /> <br /> Meerlinda is directing the project, and working with the family tree and histories run by the Mormons out of Salt Lake City, and she is keeping tabs on the results of the humane genome project.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that first appeared in Nights of Prophecy, but I highly doubt they got up to Antediluvian human names, and, after knowing of their vulnerability after millennia of knowledge of Blood Sorcery, I guess they'd had done something about it.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T13:12:16-08:00","id":1285047,"title":"","content":"The &quot;True Name&quot; business with the Tremere is like the plot of the Giovanni - it's always near completion, just a few more years and they will have it. If they had it now, then it's game over for everyone else; the Tremere (or Giovanni) have won the jyhad. Also, I don't think it was ever supposed to be the individual true name of every person ever but rather the aggregate true name of humanity as a species.<br /> <br /> In any case, that is what Meerlinda was working on before the Fall of Vienna, and it is probably what Tremere himself is after now. What other options are left to him?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T13:18:53-08:00","id":1285353,"title":"","content":"I guess, as far as plans go, the Mormon Project is not a bad one. But it seems to be in its very early stages, including mystically speaking. How representative of Humanity are these compiled lineages? There seems to be much research still to be done for it to reach any possibility of success. I guess it was more of a throw-away idea in one book (or in-universe, a wishful idea on Meerlinda's part) than a sure plan to invest all resources and hopes into.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T09:09:50-07:00","id":1398797,"title":"","content":"You should add that Strauss returned to LA 2018 because Prinz Vannevar Thomas appointed him as the Keeper of Elysium there as it is said in L.A. by night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}